帮助我写成这本书的，绝大部分是我以前的台积电同事。

以下是我衷心感谢的人士：

秦永沛、米玉杰、黄仁昭、方淑华——这几位现任的台积电重要经理人，提供了若干本书内容的建议。

孙又文——这位在我熟悉的人之中拥有最多学位的前台积电「投资人关系及公共关系」经理，也读了我初稿的大部分，她建议的修辞改进非常宝贵。

王建光——前台积电经理人，提供了九○年代台积电的建厂纪录。

Rick Cassidy——台积电前北美市场负责人，提供了早期美国市场的资料。

黄启烈——财务处处长，提供了关于台积电股票的资料，也提供了开发基金及飞利浦投资台积电的获利资讯。

方略——世界先进董事长，提供了若干「第二十三章」的资料。

天下文化编辑部的总编辑吴佩桥和副总编辑黄安妮尽心地做了编辑工作，而且设计了很美观的封面以及套装。

最后，我必须感谢天下文化创办人高希均及董事長王力行。几乎三十年前，高创办人鼓励我写「自传上册」；写了「上册」后，当然必须写「下冊」，他为我製造了好几年的写作苦工，但也让我重温少年的作者梦。

<div class="rebook-translation">
<span class="rebook-translation__label">ReadShift 双语翻译</span>
<p class="en-para">The vast majority of those who helped me write this book are my former TSMC colleagues.</p>
<p class="en-para">I am deeply grateful to the following people:</p>
<p class="en-para">Yung-pei Chin, Yu-chieh Mi, Jen-chao Huang, and Shu-hua Fang—these four current TSMC executives provided suggestions on portions of the book's content.</p>
<p class="en-para">Fu-wen Sun—who among those I know holds the most advanced degrees—served as TSMC's manager of investor and public relations. She read most of my draft, and her suggestions for rhetorical improvement were invaluable.</p>
<p class="en-para">Chien-kuang Wang—a former TSMC executive—provided records of TSMC's fab construction in the 1990s.</p>
<p class="en-para">Rick Cassidy—who led TSMC's North American marketing—provided early information on the U.S. market.</p>
<p class="en-para">Chi-lieh Huang—director of the finance division—provided materials on TSMC stock, as well as information on the profits earned by the Development Fund and Philips from their investments in TSMC.</p>
<p class="en-para">Fang-lueh—chairman of United Microelectronics Corporation (UMC)—provided material for 'Chapter 23.'</p>
<p class="en-para">Pei-chiao Wu, editor-in-chief, and An-i Huang, associate editor, of the Commonwealth Magazine editorial team, worked diligently on the editing and designed the beautiful cover and binding.</p>
<p class="en-para">Finally, I must thank Commonwealth Magazine's founder Hsi-chun Kao and chairman Li-hsing Wang. Nearly thirty years ago, Founder Kao encouraged me to write the first volume of my autobiography. Having written the 'first volume,' it was of course necessary to write the 'second volume.' He gave me years of laborious writing, but also allowed me to revisit the authorial dream of my youth.</p>
</div>
